    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0788" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">371.115 St 2/127</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Rumania
                        (Wilson)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-11-10">November 10,
                        1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to the Legation’s
                    despatch No. 1087 of June 30, 1933, regarding the decision of the Rumanian
                    Government to suspend payment of coupons on War Damage Bonds and particularly to
                    that portion of the Legation’s communication of June 30, 1933, to Mr. Mironescu,
                    Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs, which read as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“It appears to be obvious that bonds issued, as these were, for damage
                            sustained are in an entirely different category from ordinary
                            interest-bearing bonds and should not, therefore, be included in the
                            general agreement arrived at with the Association of Foreign
                            Bondholders.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The Department encloses in this connection certain self-explanatory
                        extracts<anchor n="38" xml:id="d484-f1"/> from a memorandum prepared in the
                    Office of the Economic Adviser.</p>
                <p>It is suggested that if a situation arises in the future similar to that under
                    reference, the Legation should request the Department for specific instructions
                    in the matter.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
